<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maiduguri</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yerwa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maiduguri is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borno-state">Borno State</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. It grew from Yerwa, the new capital founded in 1907 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abubakar-garbai">Shehu Abubakar Garbai</a> of Borno under British rule, and remains the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shehu-of-borno">Shehu of Borno</a>. It is the largest city of north-eastern Nigeria and a trading centre for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-chad">Lake Chad</a> region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maiduguri.jpg" alt="Maiduguri" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ifeatu Nnaobi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indimi_Mosque_Maiduguri_Borno_State_Nigeria.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
